specs={
'pteridinium':dict(url='https://doi.org/10.1017/pab.2022.2',pixels=['pteridinium-page2.png','pteridinium-page6.png'],dims=[.20,.075,.045],palette={'fossil':'#B18D62','matrix':'#8B7151'},features=['Three longitudinal quilted vanes meet at common seam','Two lateral vanes curve into canoe cavity and converge at both ends','Offset tubular module relief across central seam, central third vane physically divides cavity','Fossil-form specimen study with small supporting matrix; third-vane posture interpretive, no complete living organism'],claim='Original genus-level Pteridinium fossil-form specimen study informed by named Pteridinium simplex material, not a scan, specimen facsimile or confident living organism reconstruction. Erniettomorph affinity remains debated. Small matrix display and third-vane height/posture are artistic interpretations.',observation='Personally read Darroch et al2022 primary description and complete Fig1/3 captions; personally viewed actual PDF p528 Fig1 SMF XXX660f dorsal/side and p532 Fig3 SMF XXX660k A-F. Fig1 shows two ribbed lateral vanes and seam with third vane absent; Fig3 D/F/E expose lateral h and medial v vanes, kinked offset modules and break along medial vane. These are fossil photographs, not CFD panels. Fossil material often distorted. UT2014 text read; CT volumes/meshes not downloaded.',decisions='Concept canoe cavity and third-vane direction useful, but bead-like dorsal ornaments and tall sail exaggerate. Build one continuous closed thin three-vane fossil volume with two upcurved lateral quilted wings, modest central upright quilted vane along common keel seam, glide-offset unbranched module relief. No dorsal beads, roots or mouth. Small irregular matrix supports lower keel; display posture inferential, not living reconstruction.'),
'pingo':dict(url='https://parks.canada.ca/lhn-nhs/nt/pingo/gestion-management/initiation-101',pixels=['pingo-photo.jpg'],dims=[36,32,13],palette={'turf':'#85865A','soil':'#9A7C56','ice':'#A8CDD5'},features=['Broad domed frost mound continuous with low flat tundra base','Narrow irregular summit tension fissures, not circular volcanic crater','One small removed side sector reveals solid ice-core teaching schematic under thin soil','Opaque faceted volume; no claim of actual exposed Ibyuk core'],claim='Generic original geological pingo process/form teaching concept informed by modern analogues. Side cutaway and ice core are explicitly schematic, not observed exposure of Ibyuk or measured internal structure. No period, named site, exact age or dimensions asserted.',observation='Personally read ParksCanada Pingos101 ice-cored hill formation, water pressure uplift and nearly pure ice core text; management Ibyuk photograph copyright ParksCanada personally viewed: rounded broad domed vegetated mound over flat tundra, narrow summit gullies/cracks, not volcanic cone. Research page separates Ibyuk monitoring from PeninsulaPoint massive ice; latter not used as direct core proof.',decisions='Concept dome and cutaway useful, but cross-view brown ring resembles arbitrary strata. Build single continuous broad faceted turf dome, three narrow branching summit grooves physically carved in height field, small front-right sector removed down through top to reveal solid pale-blue schematic ice section under thin brown soil contact. No circular crater or broad natural exposed ice claim. Base continuous with flat surrounding tundra.'),
'sill-ledge':dict(url='https://home.nps.gov/glac/learn/nature/geologicformations.htm',pixels=['sill-photo.jpg'],dims=[12,7,7],palette={'host':'#B7A080','sill':'#535A5A','baked':'#D7C9AA','hostshade':'#9D896E'},features=['Substantial dark tabular igneous intrusion parallel to gently dipping host beds','Resistant projecting physical ledge and broken blocky joint faces','Pale narrow baked contacts above and below dark intrusive body','Several subordinate host beds, no crosscutting vertical dike or coal recolor'],claim='Generic original geological sill exposure teaching outcrop informed by PurcellSill modern exposure. No named locality replica, exact composition, dimensions, period or age asserted. Contact margins and erosion stylized.',observation='Personally read NPS Glacier description of magma intruding between SiyehLimestone beds, dark diorite sill and white marble contact zones; personally viewed actual NPS Sexton/Going-to-the-SunMountain photograph showing dark resistant continuous near-bedding band with pale margins through layered host. Also general NPS intrusive definition read. No imported reference mesh/texture.',decisions='Concept resistant sill and parallel contact bands useful; excessive phototexture and repeated blocks not retained. Build integrated full-volume layered outcrop, shared dipping contacts, thick dark sill protruding beyond recessed host, shallow uneven physical joints in exposed sill face and several host bedding ledges. No individual intersecting blocks or random painted seam.'),
'exfoliation-dome':dict(url='https://www.nps.gov/yose/learn/nature/geology-exhibits.htm',pixels=['dome-sentinel.jpg','dome-photo.png','dome-wide.png'],dims=[14,12,8],palette={'granite':'#AAA59A','sheet':'#BCB6A8','edge':'#918D83'},features=['One coherent rounded massive granite dome with mostly continuous crown','Two or three broad irregular curved outer sheets peel locally from shoulder','Sheets conform to dome with tapered margins and physical undercut gaps','No regular stacked circular tiers, horizontal bedding or repeated scales'],claim='Generic original exfoliation-dome geological form concept informed by modern granite analogues. No named dome replica, age, locality or exact dimensions asserted. Broad local sheets stylized, not mechanical onion layers or a claim HalfDome split in one event.',observation='Personally read NPS Yosemite distinction between regional joints and smaller curved exfoliation joints. Personally viewed NPGallery RalphHAnderson SentinelDome RL_00730 photograph: one broad curved exfoliation shell with raised broken edge following continuous bedrock slope. Actual combined diagram/right HalfDome joints photo viewed separately from diagram; actual HalfDome wide photo shows rounded massive body, not literal missing half event. Archive asset constraints Publicdomain with conditional copyright notice; all pixels consult-only. AllenGlazner right-side credit retained for exhibit image.',decisions='Concept rounded dome useful but detached shoulder pieces too blade-like and regular. Build coherent rounded ellipsoidal granite body with only two broad curved asymmetric sheet patches, strongly conformal to shoulder with modest undercut gap, varying irregular edge shape/thickness. Core remains continuous beneath patches. No horizontal repeated tiers or scales.')}
